        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right knee pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Pain just below the patella; 2–3/10 at baseline and up to 6–7/10 with jumping, ladders, or change of direction; especially sore after work and basketball."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right knee symptom history"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Wakes 1–2 times per week after big days due to pain. No giving way, locking, or catching; no true swelling, but occasionally feels puffy after a game."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right knee examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No deformity, erythema, or effusion. Localised tenderness at the mid-to-proximal patellar tendon just inferior to the patella. Full range of motion, with mild pain at end flexion and on resisted extension. Ligaments stable; McMurray negative. Single-leg decline squat reproduces typical tendon pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
